{"title":"Integral","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>integral</b> is one of the two base concepts of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Calculus\" title=\"Calculus\">calculus</a>, along with the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Derivative\" title=\"Derivative\">derivative</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Beginner_Level\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Beginner Level</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Indefinite_Integral\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Indefinite Integral</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Notation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Rules_of_Indefinite_Integrals\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Rules of Indefinite Integrals</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Definite_Integral\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Definite Integral</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Definition_and_Notation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Definition and Notation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Rules_of_Definite_Integrals\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Rules of Definite Integrals</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Formal_Use\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Formal Use</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Riemann_Integral\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Riemann Integral</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Darboux_Integral\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Darboux Integral</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Other_Definitions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Other Definitions</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Disambiguation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Disambiguation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Beginner_Level\">Beginner Level</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Beginner Level\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In introductory, high-school level texts, the integral is often presented in two parts, the <b>indefinite integral</b> and <b>definite integral</b>. Although this approach lacks mathematical formality, it has the advantage of being easy to grasp and convenient to use in most of its applications, especially in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Physics\" title=\"Physics\">Physics</a>.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Indefinite_Integral\">Indefinite Integral</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Indefinite Integral\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The indefinite integral, or antiderivative, is a partial <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Inverse\" title=\"Inverse\">inverse</a> of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Derivative\" title=\"Derivative\">derivative</a>. That is, if the  derivative of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Function\" title=\"Function\">function </a><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/a/bbad379658bd32e9b6479bbd666b93a96e6b48ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, then the indefinite integral of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/a/bbad379658bd32e9b6479bbd666b93a96e6b48ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/c/9ac4d467ec8c0271a173cebbc2c0fa61182a9c9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Real\">real</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Constant\" title=\"Constant\">constant</a>. This is because the derivative of a constant is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notation\">Notation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Notation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li>The integral of a function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4cdb4ed11fb9d49446b111d51d20f10f4149e39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int f(x)\\,dx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"78\" height=\"39\" />, where the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/3/953640113c8002037caa26af92570f9cb7d5773c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$dx$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> means that the function is being integrated in relation to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.</li>\n<li>Often, to save space, the integral of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de8fdaa56ea5a8940d4bba79faa9e3dea0f6bf7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" />, the integral of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/7/1f745cf4286f88b236750e1e9a8abe3dacd9dc39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/4/df4e0c1b626e2abd358c8aa60271a28778f866e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" />, etc.</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Rules_of_Indefinite_Integrals\">Rules of Indefinite Integrals</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Rules of Indefinite Integrals\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/0/c3044a43f4831402fde270f95290876d9a87895d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int c\\,dx=cx+C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"130\" height=\"39\" /> for a constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and another constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/6/e16bea40e04e8f3db71565d95cef3042f3cb1a5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int f(x)+g(x)...+z(x)\\,dx=\\int f(x)\\,dx+\\int g(x)\\,dx...+\\int z(x)\\,dx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"524\" height=\"39\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/5/43594a91a1a17ac25c040b2db326ac22e870db74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int x^n\\,dx=\\frac{1}{n+1}x^{n+1}+C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"206\" height=\"39\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0a14bfbe708a6cdf5d6961a5ca917965caba76d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ne -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"17\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/0/36046c842c3171e5f651f40aad69ca1c116916e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int x^{-1}\\,dx=\\ln |x|+C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"171\" height=\"39\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/9/0593fa1067ce776df9c29aefd153ad3d556a1662.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int \\sin x\\,dx = -\\cos x + C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"195\" height=\"39\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/6/7768147dab5c8fe655a2443ee1492ecfc51a82f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int \\cos x\\,dx = \\sin x + C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"177\" height=\"39\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/d/85d86cf90a2b9075cb69bbbb5fb2364f7634fe49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int\\tan x\\,dx =  \\ln |\\cos x| + C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"213\" height=\"39\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac46d0bd16c5e4bff3b019e732c46e80b468a525.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int \\sec x\\,dx = \\ln |\\sec x + \\tan x| + C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"273\" height=\"42\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/8/428036342fbdc9d1ffc7c0e6d9803f6d29eecfe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int \\csc \\, dx =\\ln |\\csc x + \\cot x| + C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"258\" height=\"39\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/0/16023bcfabb61a1929daae0135c24696ec667fb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int \\cot x\\,dx = \\ln |\\sin x| + C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"209\" height=\"39\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/d/e9de8cb46dc0679e8cca667277ea14e7e5dfa6c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int cf(x)\\, dx=c\\int f(x)\\,dx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"201\" height=\"39\" /></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Definite_Integral\">Definite Integral</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Definite Integral\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The definite integral is also the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">area</a> under a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Curve\" title=\"Curve\">curve</a> between two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Points\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Points\">points</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. For example, the area under the curve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/5/545d56fae6182fc4170005c18a8a808b325a7f75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=\\sin x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/4/ba41f0f71a21421a018e06291611e43abfe58876.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"27\" height=\"33\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aeebb746f8c0d3dac5219c3635617032430afee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"17\" height=\"34\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, as area below the x-axis is taken as negative area. \n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Definition_and_Notation\">Definition and Notation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Definition and Notation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li>The definite integral of a function between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/0/fc02ba374914483c95dd803c7cb783a5cb7e5672.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int^{b}_{a}f(x)\\,dx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"85\" height=\"44\" />.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/6/30620848416d4a0c98fdb9ce96077f741b09b618.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int^{b}_{a}f(x)\\,dx=F(b)-F(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"204\" height=\"44\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de8fdaa56ea5a8940d4bba79faa9e3dea0f6bf7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> is the antiderivative of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />. This is also notated <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/4/f842e26fbd63bf550f28b6786af1da466525bd86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\int f(x)\\,dx]^{b}_{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"96\" height=\"39\" />, read as \"The integral of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> evaluated at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.\" Note that this means in definite integration, one need not add a constant, as the constants from the functions cancel out.</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Rules_of_Definite_Integrals\">Rules of Definite Integrals</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Rules of Definite Integrals\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/5/fb5e1b7bbcc2395b9635142127933c5fc7ffc85e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int^{b}_{a}f(x)\\,dx=\\int^{b}_{c}f(x)\\,dx+\\int^{c}_{a}f(x)\\,dx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"303\" height=\"44\" /> for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>Also,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/6/ad6963fe6c7881b45b7f7a0a33b633b10c909f82.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Area} = \\iint f(x, y)\\,dA\\]\" width=\"163\" height=\"30\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/0/9208b757bb00d76189e6aef01105fbc130a1ce9f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Vol} = \\iiint f(x, y, z)\\,dV\\]\" width=\"180\" height=\"30\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/d/5bd260a8dc329fe425bcd202e25288f594fcd3d4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{4V} = \\iiiint f(x, y, z, w)\\,dV\\]\" width=\"219\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Formal_Use\">Formal Use</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Formal Use\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The notion of an <b>integral</b> is one of the key ideas in severel areas of higher mathematics including <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Analysis\" title=\"Analysis\">analysis</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Topology\" title=\"Topology\">topology</a>. The integral can be defined in several ways which can be applied to several different settings. However, the most common definition, and the one which most closely resembles the the 'definite integral' is the <b>Riemann Integral</b>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Riemann_Integral\">Riemann Integral</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Riemann Integral\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/c/67c320754a36aaec178e61f04bfcbac41c0bf675.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:[a,b]\\rightarrow\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/2/04295f8531b51cd23b0dc3c796c42e622e6370ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L\\in\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>We say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is <b>Riemann Integrable</b> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecbd1ba3da8f2adef66a63f2ab32c47e63fa734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> if and only if\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/3/7e311f2bc88a3b2eeec3664581efd60a2e9ad08c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall \\epsilon&gt;0\\:\\exists\\delta&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"106\" height=\"13\" /> such that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/e/d7e0599a6618d30957619f214699749da9938ad7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{\\dot{P}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Partition\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Partition\">tagged partition</a> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecbd1ba3da8f2adef66a63f2ab32c47e63fa734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/5/755bb1cabe2b24ca4142a9096f3b3f5fab9fcfcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\|\\mathcal{\\dot{P}}\\|&lt;\\delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"21\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/4/ef48ac956824fcaea163a530a717e6df694aa006.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/2/e220c3b41713e0aec02f90f25b89f9292720d95e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S(f,\\mathcal{\\dot{P}})-L|&lt;\\epsilon$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"21\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/8/ce83a25b9b3e29c29826cbf380eccfc7080abcc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(f,\\mathcal{\\dot{P}})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"21\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Riemann_sum\" title=\"Riemann sum\">Riemann sum</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/e/d7e0599a6618d30957619f214699749da9938ad7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{\\dot{P}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is said to be the <b>integral</b> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecbd1ba3da8f2adef66a63f2ab32c47e63fa734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> and is written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8daef930e29a264cf7d6cddf545c639a6cebbb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L=\\int_a^b f(x)dx=\\int_a^b f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"184\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>&lt;geogebra&gt;2f3876024e3b8d9e4506f2173c591cbfaca665de&lt;/geogebra&gt;\n</p><p>Another integral commonly used in introductory texts is the <b>Darboux Integral</b> (which is often called the Riemann Integral)\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Darboux_Integral\">Darboux Integral</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Darboux Integral\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/c/67c320754a36aaec178e61f04bfcbac41c0bf675.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:[a,b]\\rightarrow\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is <b>Darboux Integrable</b> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecbd1ba3da8f2adef66a63f2ab32c47e63fa734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/8/698c5d302d50604a842f1935daf84ae2558818fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\inf_{\\mathcal{P}}U(f,\\mathcal{P})=\\sup_{\\mathcal{P}}L(f,\\mathcal{P})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"197\" height=\"29\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/9/1c9a4456eb41d63a8be2f49f848508c85931a159.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L(f,\\mathcal{P})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/0116bd434902261307d5892bed0019de2424d7d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U(f,\\mathcal{P})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> are respectively the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Riemann_sum\" title=\"Riemann sum\">lower sum</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Riemann_sum\" title=\"Riemann sum\">upper sum</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> with respect to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Partition\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Partition\">partition</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f4008768812f46db4b252c9e69cf98c5faaa4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{P}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>The notation used for the Darboux integral is the same as that for the Riemann integral. \n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Integral&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Other_Definitions\">Other Definitions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Other Definitions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Other important definitions of integration include the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Riemann-Stieltjes_integral&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Riemann-Stieltjes integral (page does not exist)\">Riemann-Stieltjes integral</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Lebesgue_integral\" title=\"Lebesgue integral\">Lebesgue integral</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Henstock-Kurzweil_integral\" title=\"Henstock-Kurzweil integral\">Henstock-Kurzweil integral</a>, etc.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Disambiguation\">Disambiguation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Disambiguation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>The word <i>integral</i> is the adjectival form of the noun \"<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integer</a>.\"  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is integral while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> is not.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Calculus\" title=\"Calculus\">Calculus</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Derivative\" title=\"Derivative\">Derivative</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Function\" title=\"Function\">Function</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Measure_theory&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Measure theory (page does not exist)\">Measure theory</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018002659\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.043 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.060 seconds\n